      "pageDescription": "Learn fact-checking skills online with Poynter. Verify claims, evaluate sources and navigate misinformation and AI-generated content.",
      "evidenceText": "Fact-Checking for Everyone - Poynter Fact-Checking for Everyone - Poynter DONATE What do you want to search? Submit Sign In | Membership News Training Ethics Fact-Checking Media Literacy AI Events Future of Public Media Newmark Ethics Center IFCN MediaWise PolitiFact Donate About Us Press Freedom Watch The Poynter 50 Podcasts Artificial Intelligence Business & Work Reporting & Editing Fact-Checking Ethics & Trust Local News Journalism, Media & Communication Training Poynter Membership Categories Consulting & Coaching For ACES Members For Local News Funders All Categories Broadcast & Visual Journalism Business & Work Ethics Fact-Checking & Media Literacy Leadership Reporting & Editing Writing Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Intermediate Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate in Editing Workshops and Coaching Tools for Funders Ethics Ethics Training Ethics Articles AI Ethics Public Editor Project Get Ethics Advice Fact-Checking Articles IFCN IFCN Grants International Fact-Checking Day Teen Creator Network PolitiFact MediaWise Media Literacy Resources AI Literacy Ambassadors Teen Creator Network Research & News International en Español MediaWise Training All Events The 2026 Poynter Journalism Prizes Oops! We could not locate your form. Sign In Register Sign into your account Sign In or Register to Enroll - OR - Checkout as a Guest Remember Me Reset Password Don't have an account? Register Sign In Register Register a new account Sign In or Register to Enroll Password should contain at least: Eight characters One uppercase letter One lowercase letter One number One of the following special characters: @ # - _ $ * % ^ & + = § ! ? Already have an account? Sign In Sign In Register Fact-Checking for Everyone $ 49.00 Fact-Checking for Everyone quantity Enroll Now Fact-Checking & Media Literacy Online Fact-Checking for Everyone Learn how to investigate claims, evaluate sources and verify what you see online using techniques from Poynter and the International Fact-Checking Network. This self-directed, three-hour course gives you a practical fact-checking process for navigating misinformation, AI-generated content and the information you encounter every day. Start Anytime Overview Learn at your own pace through six self-directed lessons on the fundamentals of fact-checking. Plan for approximately three hours to complete the course. Practice your skills with real-world examples, case studies, quizzes, reflections and exercises. Apply what you learn at work, school, in your writing, content creation or everyday life. Enroll for $49 and get started when you’re ready. Fact-Checking for Everyone quantity Enroll Now SKU: 82618 Tags: Fact-checking , front page course , ifcn , online Learning Outcomes In this course, participants will: Understand how digital information environments influence what people see and believe. Recognize when information deserves a closer look before accepting or sharing it. Analyze claims, sources and evidence to make well-supported judgments. Develop a systematic approach to investigating information and reaching conclusions. Gain confidence evaluating information across digital platforms and emerging technologies. Apply standards of accuracy, fairness and transparency when sharing what they find. $ 49.00 Fact-Checking for Everyone quantity Enroll Now Overview Learn at your own pace through six self-directed lessons on the fundamentals of fact-checking. Plan for approximately three hours to complete the course. Practice your skills with real-world examples, case studies, quizzes, reflections and exercises. Apply what you learn at work, school, in your writing, content creation or everyday life. Enroll for $49 and get started when you’re ready. Training 5 or More People? get consulting & coaching Description Schedule Requirements A viral photo, a link shared in the group chat or a confident answer from an AI chatbot can all leave us with the same question: How do we know what to trust? Knowing how to find the answer is no longer just a journalism skill. It’s a life skill. Fact-Checking for Everyone gives you practical tools to investigate claims, evaluate sources and make more informed decisions about the information you encounter daily. Learn a fact-checking process you can use anywhere In this 100% self-directed course, you’ll learn how to spot a fact-checkable claim, weigh the credibility of a source and trace information back to where it started, the core moves professional fact-checkers use every day. Through real-world examples and hands-on exercises, you’ll build your own trusted source database and develop a repeatable fact-checking methodology you can use at work, at school and in everyday life. Why learn with Poynter? Created by the team behind Poynter’s International Fact-Checking Network (IFCN), this course draws on the techniques and principles used by professional fact-checkers around the world. It brings together expertise from across Poynter, including the IFCN, PolitiFact , and MediaWise . You’ll learn the principles that guide professional fact-checking, including accuracy, fairness and transparency, translated into practical skills anyone can use. Questions? If you need assistance, email us at info@poynter.org . This is a 100% self-directed, online course you can begin anytime. The course includes six lessons and takes approximately three hours to complete. You’ll have access to the complete course materials so you can work through lessons at your own pace. Here’s how the course breaks down: Lesson 1: How information works in a digital age Explore how information spreads and how emotion, algorithms and confirmation bias shape what we believe. Lesson 2: What makes it a fact? Identify fact-checkable claims, distinguish facts from opinions and recognize when important context is missing. Lesson 3: Verification and fact-checking Practice lateral reading, evaluate sources, spot red flags and build a repeatable fact-checking methodology. Lesson 4: AI chatbots and fact-checking Investigate chatbot-provided sources, spot common errors and verify AI-generated information. Lesson 5: Essential digital tools Use tools and techniques to verify images, videos, websites and social media content. Lesson 6: Fact-checking standards and ethics Present findings accurately using principles of fairness, attribution, transparency and accountability. Fact-checking for Everyone is designed for anyone who wants to make smarter decisions about the information they encounter. The course may be especially useful for: People who work in journalism organizations, including audience, production, administrative and other non-reporting roles Writers, associate producers and communications professionals College students and other learners strengthening their research and media literacy skills Content creators who want to improve the accuracy and credibility of what they publish Anyone who wants practical tools for navigating news, social media, AI-generated content and everyday claims Cost $49 Instructors Angie Drobnic Holan Director, International Fact-Checking Network Angie Drobnic Holan is the director of the International Fact-Checking Network, which supports and promotes fact-checking worldwide. Before assuming that role in June 2023, Holan... Read More Alanna Dvorak International Training Manager Alanna Dvorak is the International Training Manager with IFCN, where she helps produce interactive learning materials for journalists around the globe. Prior to her current... Read More \"> Related Products Certificate Online Getting It Right: Accuracy and Verification in the Digital Age $ 50.00 Certificate Online AI for Journalists and Content Creators: From Understanding to Application $ 95.00 Sale Online How Any Journalist Can Earn Trust (International Edition) $ 50.00 Original price was: $50.00. $ 0.00 Current price is: $0.00. Free Online COVID conspiracies, flu facts and respiratory r